      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "99% of VRC players do not check world menus. They will hardly use them and just end up complaining unless someone shows them \"hey there is a very obvious world menu that you keep running past that's really NOT hard to miss\" is one of my favorites. \n\nGesture based menu toggles are.. cool.. but can annoying and tedious. It's recommended to throw up a message in someones face the moment they join because if it's not directly in their face, they will not notice it\n\nRant over\n\nAlso they do have desktop controls for menus. It's up to the world creator to add that functionality",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-05-12T17:43:46.463Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "World menus have naturally clustered around some common approaches to access for VR (like reaching behind head or pulling hands apart) which is great for making it easy for users to intuitively check for menus when they visit new worlds without having to search for instructions. But these hand actions are either very difficult or simply not possible on desktop, resulting in either menus not being as portable for desktop users, or having very \"cluttered\" interfaces with world-specific keybindings. This could be simplified by adding a key binding to desktop for the common menu-access actions like \"reaching behind head\" and \"pulling hands apart in front of player\". That way, players on desktop can enjoy the same ease of use.",
